class.description:
DisPdu is a collection of static methods shared by all PDU classes; it is not instantiated. Use [method peek_header] to read the 12-byte header without decoding the body, and [method decode] to turn a received packet into the matching [DisPduBase] subclass.
All input is validated before it is parsed, so a malformed packet makes [method decode] return [code]null[/code] instead of failing; the reason is available from [method get_last_error].
[codeblock]
func _on_packet(bytes: PackedByteArray) -> void:
	var header := DisPdu.peek_header(bytes)
	if header.is_empty() or not DisPdu.is_supported(header["pdu_type"]):
		return
	var pdu := DisPdu.decode(bytes)
	if pdu == null:
		push_warning("Bad PDU: " + DisPdu.get_last_error())
		return
	if pdu is DisFirePdu:
		print("Fired by ", pdu.firing_entity_id)
[/codeblock]
[b]Note:[/b] [DisNetwork] already decodes incoming packets and emits signals; call these methods directly only when you read packets yourself, for example from a file.
